      "side": 1,
      "message": "tl;dr; it\u0027s unsafe only for libraries that set the unsafe_* flag\n\nIt\u0027s a special path that kicks in when Ignore_missing_latest_api is set (and it is only set in java_sdk_library\u0027s use-case, Ignore_missing_latest_api is \"mutated\"). There are many java_sdk_library\u0027s that don\u0027t have last_released API files checked in. \n\nhttp://r.android.com/1534347 changes the behavior of java_sdk_library to no longer allow this by default. They must now set the attr Unsafe_ignore_missing_latest_api to get this behavior. There are a handful of of java_sdk_libraries that don\u0027t really need this sort of tracking, so I took that route rather than adding some bogus last-released files for them.\n\nLet me know if you have a suggestion for how to better deal with it",
